From 7b9ea3550cb00ed3beb889c6f47da7540cca3dfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:01:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/27] wifi: ath12k: Add support for the peach (WCN7880) chip

Kaanapali phones such as the Nubia RedMagic 11 Pro use Qualcomm's
"peach" Wi-Fi 7 chip (PCI 17cb:110e, firmware variant WCN7880, family
"Ganges"). The downstream host driver treats it like WCN7850 ("kiwi")
for its copy engines, target definitions and shadow registers, so it is
added as a WCN7850 variant with these differences, all taken from the
downstream cnss2 driver:

- The register window control is at 0x3278 (as on QCC2072); with
  WCN7850's 0x310c every windowed access reads 0xffffffff.
- aux_ucode is downloaded, and the host capability feature list carries
  WLAN_EN_SUPPORT and AUX_UC_SUPPORT but not QDSS_CFG_MISS. Without a
  QDSS trace configuration to wait for, the firmware completes its init
  right after the M3 info, rejects the aux_ucode (QMI error 90) and
  asserts about 160 ms later. Add the QDSS trace config download (QMI
  0x44, qdss_trace_config.cfg), used when QDSS_CFG_MISS is not set.
- Cold boot calibration: run the firmware in calibration mode (7) first,
  then power cycle it into mission mode with cal_done set and CALDB
  kept, as downstream does (qcom,wlan-cbc-enabled). Powering down after
  a calibration-only boot needs ath12k_pci_power_down() to also run when
  only MHI is up.

Firmware files (from the phone's vendor partitions) in
ath12k/PEACH/hw2.0: amss.bin (amss20.bin), m3.bin (phy_ucode20.elf),
aux_ucode.bin (aux_ucode20.elf), board.bin (bdwlan.elf), regdb.bin and
qdss_trace_config.cfg (qdss_trace_config_v2.cfg).

Tested: calibration takes 8.3 s as on Android, then wlan0 scans 2.4 and
5 GHz networks. Connecting has not been tested yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
